# Go standard library vulnerabilities that require upgrading to Go 1.25+
# v8go (CGO binding to V8 engine) currently requires Go 1.23
# These will be resolved when v8go supports Go 1.25+
# Tracked: https://github.com/nicholasgasior/v8go/issues

# crypto/tls - ECH privacy leak (Go 1.25.12)
CVE-2026-46597

# crypto/x509 - inefficient hostname parsing (Go 1.25.11)
CVE-2026-39830

# crypto/x509 - unexpected work during chain building (Go 1.25.9)
CVE-2026-39831

# crypto/x509 - inefficient policy validation (Go 1.25.9)
CVE-2026-39832

# crypto/tls - unauthenticated KeyUpdate record (Go 1.25.9)
CVE-2026-39835

# net - panic in Dial/LookupPort with NUL on Windows (Go 1.25.10)
CVE-2026-39828

# net/textproto - arbitrary inputs in errors (Go 1.25.11)
CVE-2026-39829

# net/http - infinite loop in HTTP/2 transport (Go 1.25.10)
CVE-2026-42508

# os - unsafe read from os.File after errors (Go 1.25.8)
CVE-2026-46595

# golang.org/x/net - SSH server DoS (fixed in x/crypto)
CVE-2025-22869

# golang.org/x/net - HTTP/2 SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE
CVE-2025-47913
